IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wrca-dates`
IMPORT `wrca-seat`

-- Workers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988 (Tas) -- cases for the worker's seat (wrca-seat.l4).
--
-- Every expected value is worked by hand from the deposited text, with the arithmetic in the comment above the
-- assertion. The basic salary is ILLUSTRATIVE: $1,200 a week (the gazetted figure is not deposited).
--
-- Mia is a full-time storeperson at a Hobart warehouse (Monday to Friday), born 15 June 1990, employed since 1 July 2020.
-- She hurts her back lifting stock on Monday 2 March 2026 and cannot work from that day. She tells her supervisor at
-- once; her claim, with its certificate, reaches the employer on Wednesday 11 March 2026; her pay day is Thursday, and
-- the first after the claim is 19 March. In the 12 months before the injury she was paid $80,000: $4,000 rostered,
-- required, uniform overtime; a $2,000 discretionary bonus; $5,000 of travel and meal allowances. Her ordinary rate is
-- $32 an hour for 38 hours. Tom, a delivery driver, dies on Monday 1 June 2026 of a work injury of 2 March 2026; his
-- partner Leo was wholly dependent on him, and their daughter Ava was born on 1 January 2012.

`BS` MEANS 1200

§ `Am I covered, and what must I do by when?`

-- Mia: a worker, not a disease, in the course of employment: liable.
#ASSERT `Is my employer liable to compensate me for this injury` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the employer is liable to pay compensation (s 25(1))`
-- Hurt driving home, not at the employer's request: not from the employment (s 25(6)(a)).
#ASSERT `Is my employer liable to compensate me for this injury` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not liable: the injury did not arise out of or in the course of the employment (s 25(1)(a), (6))`
-- A contractor, not a worker: not liable.
#ASSERT `Is my employer liable to compensate me for this injury` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not liable: the person is not the employer's worker (s 3(1))`
-- A farmhand with brucellosis caught from the employer's cattle (the work the major factor), but no doctor's written
-- certificate on a blood test: not liable (s 25(2)(b)). With the certificate: liable.
#ASSERT `Is my employer liable to compensate me for this injury` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not liable: undulant fever or brucellosis without a medical practitioner's written certificate on the blood examination (s 25(2)(b))`
#ASSERT `Is my employer liable to compensate me for this injury` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the employer is liable to pay compensation (s 25(1))`
-- A heart attack on shift, given as an injury in the course of employment, the work not the major factor: not liable
-- (s 25(2)(ba)).
#ASSERT `Is my employer liable to compensate me for this injury` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not liable: a heart condition or aneurism to which the employment was not the major or most significant factor (s 25(2)(ba), s 3(2A))`
-- Injured 2 March 2026: claim by 2 September 2026 (6 months).
#ASSERT `By when must I make my claim` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE TRUE (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) EQUALS `the claim must be made on or before` (`the calendar date` 2 9 2026)
-- Industrial deafness, left the job on 31 August 2026: by 28 February 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must I make my claim` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) TRUE FALSE (`the calendar date` 31 8 2026) EQUALS `the claim must be made on or before` (`the calendar date` 28 2 2027)
-- Her claim on 11 March: in time. A claim on 3 September: out of time; but valid if late because the employer never gave
-- the s 33A notice (s 38(2)(aa)).
#ASSERT `Is my claim in time` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE TRUE (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the claim is in time (s 32)`
#ASSERT `Is my claim in time` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE TRUE (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 3 9 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the claim is out of time: no entitlement to compensation (s 32(1)(b))`
#ASSERT `Is my claim in time` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE TRUE (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 3 9 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the claim is late but valid: the failure was occasioned by mistake, absence from the State or other reasonable cause (s 38)`
-- She told her supervisor at once, before leaving: notice given.
#ASSERT `Did I give notice of my injury as required` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `notice was given as s 32(1)(a) requires`
-- Told 2 March: the employer must give her the right-to-claim notice by 16 March.
#ASSERT `By when must my employer tell me of my right to claim` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `the employer must inform the worker of the right to claim, in the Schedule 1 form, on or before` (`the calendar date` 16 3 2026)
-- Claim received 11 March: the status notice by 8 April (28 days).
#ASSERT `By when must I be told whether my claim is accepted` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 8 4 2026
-- First pay day Thursday 19 March, 8 days on, and practicable: payments by 19 March. Not practicable: by 25 March.
#ASSERT `By when must my weekly payments start` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 19 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS `the calendar date` 19 3 2026
#ASSERT `By when must my weekly payments start` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 19 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `the calendar date` 25 3 2026
-- Incapacity from 2 March, claim given 11 March (14 days before is 25 February): payable from 2 March.
#ASSERT `From what date are my weekly payments payable` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 2 3 2026
-- No dispute by 4 June 2026 (the 84 days ran to 3 June): taken to have accepted. On 1 May: not yet; until 3 June.
#ASSERT `Is my employer taken to have accepted liability for my claim` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 4 6 2026) EQUALS `liability is taken to have been accepted (s 81AB)`
#ASSERT `Is my employer taken to have accepted liability for my claim` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 5 2026) EQUALS `not yet decided: the employer may still dispute liability on or before` (`the calendar date` 3 6 2026)

§ `What is my weekly payment, how does it step down, and when does it stop?`

-- Normal weekly earnings: 80,000 - 4,000 - 2,000 - 5,000 + 4,000 (the overtime counts) = 73,000 over the 365 days to
-- 2 March 2026: 73,000 / (365 / 7) = 1,400.
#ASSERT `What are my normal weekly earnings` (`the calendar date` 1 7 2020) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) 80000 4000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 2000 5000 FALSE 0 `none of the contracts is full-time` FALSE 0 30 40 EQUALS 1400
-- The overtime not uniform: left out, 69,000 x 7 / 365.
#ASSERT `What are my normal weekly earnings` (`the calendar date` 1 7 2020) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) 80000 4000 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 2000 5000 FALSE 0 `none of the contracts is full-time` FALSE 0 30 40 EQUALS 483000 DIVIDED BY 365
-- Total incapacity: the greater of 1,400 and 32 x 38 = 1,216: 1,400.
#ASSERT `What is my weekly payment before any step-down` 1400 TRUE TRUE 32 38 0 0 EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1400
-- Back on suitable duties earning 500: partial, 1,400 - 500 = 900.
#ASSERT `What is my weekly payment before any step-down` 1400 TRUE FALSE 32 38 0 500 EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 900
-- The award rate rises 1.50 an hour: 1,400 + 1.50 x 38 = 1,457.
#ASSERT `What is my weekly payment before any step-down` 1400 TRUE TRUE 32 38 1.50 0 EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1457
-- No certificate: nothing.
#ASSERT `What is my weekly payment before any step-down` 1400 FALSE TRUE 32 38 0 0 EQUALS `no weekly payment: the incapacity is not supported by a certificate in the form the Board approved (s 69(1))`
-- Stop: impairment not assessed, 9 years after 2 March 2026: 2 March 2035 (before her pension age, 15 June 2057).
#ASSERT `When does my entitlement to weekly payments stop` (`the calendar date` 15 6 1990) 67 (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE 0 EQUALS `the entitlement to weekly payments ceases on` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2035) `9 years after the initial incapacity (s 69B(1)(c)(i), (2E)(a))`
-- Assessed at 32%: the s 87 day, her 67th birthday, 15 June 2057.
#ASSERT `When does my entitlement to weekly payments stop` (`the calendar date` 15 6 1990) 67 (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) TRUE 32 EQUALS `the entitlement to weekly payments ceases on` (`the calendar date` 15 6 2057) `the worker attains the pension age (s 87(1)(a))`
-- Step-downs for an unbroken incapacity from Monday 2 March 2026: Monday 31 August 2026 and Monday 30 August 2027.
#ASSERT (`When does my weekly payment step down` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026))'s `the first day at 90% (or 95%)` EQUALS `the calendar date` 31 8 2026
#ASSERT (`When does my weekly payment step down` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026))'s `the first day at 80% (or 85%)` EQUALS `the calendar date` 30 8 2027

-- Mia's week, with her other facts: 38 ordinary hours and 2 hours of overtime that counts (normal weekly hours 40),
-- full-time, a basic salary of 1,200, pension age 67, not assessed.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, first IS A DATE, unusual IS A BOOLEAN, suitable IS A BOOLEAN, notoffered IS A BOOLEAN, planhours IS A NUMBER, earned IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Weekly payment answer`
`Mia's week` n first unusual suitable notoffered planhours earned MEANS
    `What is my weekly payment for this week` 1400 n first unusual suitable notoffered planhours earned FALSE FALSE TRUE 38 0 0 2 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 38 38 `BS` (`the calendar date` 15 6 1990) 67 (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE 0

-- Week 10: 1,400. Week 30: 90%, 1,260. Week 30 unfit for usual duties, fit for suitable duties not offered: 95%, 1,330.
#ASSERT `Mia's week` 10 (`the calendar date` 4 5 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1400
#ASSERT `Mia's week` 30 (`the calendar date` 21 9 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1260
#ASSERT `Mia's week` 30 (`the calendar date` 21 9 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 0 EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1330
-- Week 30 working 20 hours under an approved return-to-work plan (50% of 40): no reduction, 1,400.
#ASSERT `Mia's week` 30 (`the calendar date` 21 9 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE 20 0 EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1400
-- Week 80: 80%, 1,120.
#ASSERT `Mia's week` 80 (`the calendar date` 6 9 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1120
-- Week 471 begins Monday 5 March 2035 (470 x 7 = 3,290 days after 2 March 2026), after the cessation on Friday 2 March
-- 2035: nothing. Week 470 begins Monday 26 February 2035 and is paid in full (finding 5).
#ASSERT (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) `plus days` (470 TIMES 7) EQUALS `the calendar date` 5 3 2035
#ASSERT `Mia's week` 471 (`the calendar date` 5 3 2035) FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 EQUALS `no weekly payment: the entitlement has ceased (s 69B(2E), s 87)`
#ASSERT `Mia's week` 470 (`the calendar date` 26 2 2035) FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1120

-- s 69B(2DA): Mia's facts, but as a police officer hurt in circumstances she would unlikely have been in had she not been
-- one: no step-down, 1,400 in week 30 and week 80. Where being an officer made no difference: 1,260 and 1,120.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, first IS A DATE, unlikely IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Weekly payment answer`
`a police officer's week` n first unlikely MEANS
    `What is my weekly payment for this week` 1400 n first FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 TRUE unlikely TRUE 38 0 0 2 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 38 38 `BS` (`the calendar date` 15 6 1990) 67 (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE 0

#ASSERT `a police officer's week` 30 (`the calendar date` 21 9 2026) TRUE EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1400
#ASSERT `a police officer's week` 80 (`the calendar date` 6 9 2027) TRUE EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1400
#ASSERT `a police officer's week` 30 (`the calendar date` 21 9 2026) FALSE EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1260
#ASSERT `a police officer's week` 80 (`the calendar date` 6 9 2027) FALSE EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1120

-- The whole schedule: 1,400; then 1,260 (90%); then 1,120 (80%); stopping 2 March 2035.
`Mia's schedule` MEANS `What will I be paid each week and until when` 1400 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE 38 38 `BS` (`the calendar date` 15 6 1990) 67 (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE 0
#ASSERT `Mia's schedule`'s `in the first 26 weeks` EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1400
#ASSERT `Mia's schedule`'s `from week 27 to week 78` EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1260
#ASSERT `Mia's schedule`'s `after week 78` EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1120
#ASSERT `Mia's schedule`'s `the first day at 90% (or 95%)` EQUALS `the calendar date` 31 8 2026
#ASSERT `Mia's schedule`'s `the first day at 80% (or 85%)` EQUALS `the calendar date` 30 8 2027
#ASSERT `Mia's schedule`'s `when the payments stop` EQUALS `the entitlement to weekly payments ceases on` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2035) `9 years after the initial incapacity (s 69B(1)(c)(i), (2E)(a))`
-- With suitable duties certified but not offered throughout: 1,400, 1,330 (95%), 1,190 (85%).
#ASSERT (`What will I be paid each week and until when` 1400 TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE 38 38 `BS` (`the calendar date` 15 6 1990) 67 (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE 0)'s `from week 27 to week 78` EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1330
#ASSERT (`What will I be paid each week and until when` 1400 TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE 38 38 `BS` (`the calendar date` 15 6 1990) 67 (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE 0)'s `after week 78` EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1190
-- Sam, casual, 20 hours of a 38-hour week, 500 a week: 500; 450 (90%); after week 78 the floor, 70% of 1,200 x 20 / 38
-- = 8,400 / 19 (442.11), above 80% (400).
`Sam's schedule` MEANS `What will I be paid each week and until when` 500 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE 20 38 `BS` (`the calendar date` 15 6 1990) 67 (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE 0
#ASSERT `Sam's schedule`'s `in the first 26 weeks` EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 500
#ASSERT `Sam's schedule`'s `from week 27 to week 78` EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 450
#ASSERT `Sam's schedule`'s `after week 78` EQUALS `a weekly payment of` (8400 DIVIDED BY 19)
-- A police officer to whom s 69B(2DA) applies: 1,400 in every band, stopping 2 March 2035.
`the officer's schedule` MEANS `What will I be paid each week and until when` 1400 FALSE 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE 38 38 `BS` (`the calendar date` 15 6 1990) 67 (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE 0
#ASSERT `the officer's schedule`'s `in the first 26 weeks` EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1400
#ASSERT `the officer's schedule`'s `from week 27 to week 78` EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1400
#ASSERT `the officer's schedule`'s `after week 78` EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1400
#ASSERT `the officer's schedule`'s `when the payments stop` EQUALS `the entitlement to weekly payments ceases on` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2035) `9 years after the initial incapacity (s 69B(1)(c)(i), (2E)(a))`
-- Ray, born 10 August 1960 (67 on 10 August 2027), injured 2 March 2026: stops 2 years after the injury, 2 March 2028.
#ASSERT (`What will I be paid each week and until when` 1400 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE 38 38 `BS` (`the calendar date` 10 8 1960) 67 (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE 0)'s `when the payments stop` EQUALS `the entitlement to weekly payments ceases on` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2028) `2 years after the injury (s 87(1)(b))`

§ `What lump sum is payable for my impairment?`

-- 12% physical: {18 + 6.1 x (12 - 5)} x 1,200 = 60.7 x 1,200 = 72,840.
#ASSERT `What lump sum is payable for my impairment` `a physical impairment` 12 FALSE `BS` EQUALS 72840
-- Psychiatric at 8%: below the 10% threshold, nothing. At 20%: {18 + 6.1 x 15} x 1,200 = 109.5 x 1,200 = 131,400.
#ASSERT `What lump sum is payable for my impairment` `a psychiatric impairment` 8 FALSE `BS` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What lump sum is payable for my impairment` `a psychiatric impairment` 20 FALSE `BS` EQUALS 131400
-- The tip of a finger at 2%: 3.2 x 1,200 x 2 = 7,680.
#ASSERT `What lump sum is payable for my impairment` `a physical impairment that is the loss of part or all of a finger or toe` 2 FALSE `BS` EQUALS 7680
-- Hearing: BHI 20% converts to 5 + 0.278 x 15 = 9.17, so 9%; the lump sum {18 + 6.1 x 4} x 1,200 = 42.4 x 1,200 = 50,880.
#ASSERT `What whole person impairment is my hearing loss` 20 EQUALS 9
#ASSERT `What lump sum is payable for my industrial deafness` 20 `BS` EQUALS 50880
#ASSERT `What lump sum is payable for my industrial deafness` 4 `BS` EQUALS 0

§ `If the worker dies: what do the dependants receive?`

-- Tom injured 2 March 2026, died 1 June 2026: the claim by 1 December 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must the dependants claim` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `the claim must be made on or before` (`the calendar date` 1 12 2026)
-- Leo wholly dependent, Ava his and Tom's child: 415 units to Leo, 415 x 1,200 = 498,000 (s 67(2)(a)).
#ASSERT `What lump sum is payable on the worker's death` `wholly dependent` 1 0 0 0 TRUE `BS` EQUALS `415 units, to the spouse or caring partner (s 67(2)(a))` 498000
-- If Ava were Tom's child from an earlier relationship: proportionate shares for Leo and Ava, 498,000 at most (s 67(2)(ab)).
#ASSERT `What lump sum is payable on the worker's death` `wholly dependent` 1 0 1 0 TRUE `BS` EQUALS `for each dependant, an amount reasonable and proportionate to the degree of dependency, 415 units at most in all (s 67(2)(ab), (b), (ba), (d), (3))` 498000
-- Leo's claim given 1 July 2026: weekly payments from 3 June 2026 (28 days before), later than the death.
#ASSERT `From what date are the spouse's weekly payments payable` (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 3 6 2026
-- Tom would have had 1,400 a week for total incapacity. Every s 67A period runs from the day after the death (finding
-- 18). On 10 June 2026: 1,400. On 30 November 2026, the 182nd day after the death and the last of the first 26 weeks:
-- still 1,400. On 1 December 2026: 90%, 1,260. On 1 March 2028: 80%, 1,120. On 1 June 2028, the last day of the 2 years:
-- 1,120. On 2 June 2028: ended.
#ASSERT `What weekly payment does the dependent spouse receive` (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 7 2026) 1400 FALSE 1 (`the calendar date` 10 6 2026) EQUALS `a weekly rate, for each claimant, of` 1400
#ASSERT `What weekly payment does the dependent spouse receive` (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 7 2026) 1400 FALSE 1 (`the calendar date` 30 11 2026) EQUALS `a weekly rate, for each claimant, of` 1400
#ASSERT `What weekly payment does the dependent spouse receive` (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 7 2026) 1400 FALSE 1 (`the calendar date` 1 12 2026) EQUALS `a weekly rate, for each claimant, of` 1260
#ASSERT `What weekly payment does the dependent spouse receive` (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 7 2026) 1400 FALSE 1 (`the calendar date` 1 3 2028) EQUALS `a weekly rate, for each claimant, of` 1120
#ASSERT `What weekly payment does the dependent spouse receive` (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 7 2026) 1400 FALSE 1 (`the calendar date` 1 6 2028) EQUALS `a weekly rate, for each claimant, of` 1120
#ASSERT `What weekly payment does the dependent spouse receive` (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 7 2026) 1400 FALSE 1 (`the calendar date` 2 6 2028) EQUALS `nothing on this day: the entitlement ended 2 years after the death (s 67A(2)(c), (4))`
-- Before Leo's payments are payable (3 June 2026, from his claim of 1 July): nothing on 2 June.
#ASSERT `What weekly payment does the dependent spouse receive` (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 7 2026) 1400 FALSE 1 (`the calendar date` 2 6 2026) EQUALS `nothing on this day: it is before the spouse's or caring partner's payments are payable (s 67A(1)(a), s 67B(3))`
-- Ava, 14 on 1 September 2026: 15% of 1,200 = 180 a week. The 13 weeks after the death are 2 June to 31 August 2026, so
-- her payments commence on 1 September 2026; nothing on 15 August.
#ASSERT `What weekly payment does a dependent child receive` (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 9 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 1 2012) FALSE TRUE `BS` EQUALS `a weekly rate, for each claimant, of` 180
#ASSERT `What weekly payment does a dependent child receive` (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) (`the calendar date` 15 8 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 1 2012) FALSE TRUE `BS` EQUALS `nothing on this day: a child's payments commence only on the expiration of 13 weeks after the death (s 67A(1)(b))`
-- On 2 January 2028 Ava is 16: a child only as a full-time student. Studying: 180. Not studying: nothing.
#ASSERT `What weekly payment does a dependent child receive` (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) (`the calendar date` 2 1 2028) (`the calendar date` 1 1 2012) TRUE TRUE `BS` EQUALS `a weekly rate, for each claimant, of` 180
#ASSERT `What weekly payment does a dependent child receive` (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) (`the calendar date` 2 1 2028) (`the calendar date` 1 1 2012) FALSE TRUE `BS` EQUALS `nothing on this day: the person is no longer a dependent child (s 65, s 67A(1)(b))`
-- The funeral cost 11,200: 9,500 is paid. Counselling for Leo and Ava, 2,500: all of it.
#ASSERT `How much is paid toward the funeral` 11200 EQUALS 9500
#ASSERT `How much is paid toward family counselling` 2500 EQUALS 2500

§ `Travelling expenses`

-- Mia's physiotherapy trips: 30 of parking and meals and 250 km at an Award rate of 0.80 (200): 230, under a prescribed
-- amount of 400, so 230.
#ASSERT `How much of my travel is paid` 30 250 0.80 400 EQUALS 230
